+# Release check blocked: libfoo artifact checksum mismatch
+
+The release check cannot pass without either restoring the correct artifact or
+obtaining an authoritative replacement manifest. This is an integrity failure,
+not a bug in `verify.py`.
+
+## What fails
+
+`python3 verify.py` reports:
+
+```
+checksum mismatch: libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz
+```
+
+`artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` (4000 bytes) hashes to:
+
+```
+fde9b2575edbefb297fa7d93738b4bb1f09b7f777d1723b90194ad53cd9bc9ce
+```
+
+but `SHA256SUMS` records:
+
+```
+7bee020ac21efb3831d920af0b8c5efe8d44cdf227ab94847f509188420356bd
+```
+
+The other two artifacts (`cli-2.0.1.zip`, `docs-2026.10.tar.gz`) match their
+manifest entries exactly.
+
+## Why this cannot be fixed here
+
+There is no source tree or build recipe in this repository from which to
+regenerate `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz`, and the artifact's contents do not correspond
+to the manifest. Rewriting the `libfoo` line in `SHA256SUMS` to match the
+present file would make the check green while publishing an artifact whose
+provenance/integrity is unknown, defeating the purpose of the release check.
+I have not changed `SHA256SUMS` or weakened `test_verify.py`.
+
+## Needs a decision/input from the release owner
+
+One of:
+
+1. Restore the authentic `artifacts/libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` (expected digest
+   `7bee020a...0356bd`) and re-run the check; or
+2. If the current artifact is known-good, regenerate `SHA256SUMS` from the
+   trusted release process/output and review why the manifest disagreed.
+
+## Fixed in this change
+
+`verify.py` had two independent bugs that were also failing CI:
+
+- It opened artifacts in text mode and hashed `a.read().encode()`. Binary
+  artifacts raised `UnicodeDecodeError` (and text-mode newline translation
+  would corrupt digests). It now reads with `"rb"`.
+- It compared the manifest digest verbatim even though manifests may use
+  uppercase hex. `test_verify.py` writes uppercase digests. Expected digests
+  are now normalized to lowercase before comparison.
+
+## Current status
+
+- `test_binary_files`: pass
+- `test_reports_missing`: pass
+- `test_release_artifacts_verify`: **fail** solely on the genuine
+  `libfoo-1.4.2.tar.gz` mismatch described above.
